+## v2.2.1: regimes, repeats and the P5 rerun
+
+Everything below the "Unit and file contract" is unchanged from v2.2 except where this section says so. The core is byte-identical to v2.2.
+
+| Item | Regime H (p = 500, 1000) | Regime L (p = 20, 30) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Case IDs | `[dev_]p0500_S{s}_r{rrr}`, `p1000_...` | `[dev_]p0020_S{s}_r{rrr}`, `p0030_...` |
+| `study`, `regime` columns | `bench20261019`, `H` | `newcampaign_lowp`, `L` |
+| Data seed base (prod / dev) | 1,410,000 and 1,510,000 / 2,410,000 and 2,510,000 (master sec. II.7) | 1,210,000 and 1,310,000 / 2,210,000 and 2,310,000 (LOWP_SPEC L.3) |
+| Fold seed base (prod / dev) | 3,410,000 and 3,510,000 / 4,410,000 and 4,510,000 | 3,210,000 and 3,310,000 / 4,210,000 and 4,310,000 |
+| Seeds | data = base + 10000*s + r; method = data + 4,000,000 | same; repeat m = 1..5: method + 1,000*m |
+| Inputs manifest | `inputs_manifest.csv` (dev: `dev_inputs_manifest.csv`) | `inputs_manifest_lowp.csv` in both trees (dev: `--study STUDY/dev`) |
+| Input record | `n`, `kind`, `scales` required; fold hash column `foldid_sha256` | INTERFACES I1: `n`, `kind`, `scales` checked when present; fold hash column `fold_sha256` |
+| Repeats | refused (no committed rule) | `SMCBVS_rep{m}.*`; `record$case$repeat_m`, `method_seed_base` |
+| `record$case` layout | v2.2's, unchanged | the LOWP runner's (v2.2 plus `repeat_m`, `method_seed_base`), unchanged |
+
+The `method_seed` column is always the seed handed to the core (with the repeat offset). Inputs and manifests carry the primary method seed.
+
+**P5 rerun (DECISIONS D11).** Run with `--p5-retry` and the PRIMARY allocation (`--mem-gb`, `--hours`); the adapter doubles both (hours, and `mem_gb`, which sets the core's memory preflight). It requires a valid primary unit with the same run ID, seed, source, policy and inputs whose rows have `v3_status = resource_limit`, and refuses anything else. Same seed. Output: `results/RUN_ID/pPPPP/CASE_ID/P5_retry/{SMCBVS|SMCBVS_rep{m}}_p5retry.{rds,csv,sha256,done}` (lock `..._p5retry.lock`), the same two-row CSV schema (its `allocation_sha256` is the doubled allocation's). The primary files are never touched and stay the primary result; the subfolder keeps the rerun out of the non-recursive case-folder scan of `code/scoring`. The rerun's RDS appends one element after `instrumentation`:
+
+`p5 = list(rule, role = "p5_retry", factor = 2, method_seed, primary = list(prefix, files_sha256 (the primary .sha256 lines), native_status, allocation, allocation_sha256, stop (primary fit$instrumentation$stop), runtime_s, started_utc, finished_utc), retry_allocation, retry_allocation_sha256)`.
+
+There is no second rerun: a rerun that stops again stays `resource_limit`, its own category. The rerun's own stop phase is in its `fit$instrumentation$stop`. `run_case.R` prints the stop phase (`where/phase/checkpoint/tier/iter/stage`) on its last stdout line; `tools/p5_scan.R` tabulates primary and rerun status and stop phase per unit and marks eligible units.
 
